          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em minimal dg-module
            (
            %a{:href => "#Roig92"}> Roig 92
            ,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Roig94"} Roig 94, section 1
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+model"} minimal model
            in the context of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy theory
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
          %p
            Hence over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebras"} dgc-algebras
            in non-positve degree, minimal dg-modules are the analogue of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+Sullivan+model"} minimal Sullivan model
            as one passes from
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebras"} dg-algebras
            to (just)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+fibration"} minimal fibration
            in some applications of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %p
            (In
            %a{:href => "#Halperin83"} Halperin 83
            it has “Koszul-Sullivan extensions” for
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/relative+Sullivan+algebras"} relative Sullivan algebras
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Throughout, let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+model"} Sullivan model
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient"} quotient
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
            by a circle action.
          %p
            We take all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differentials"} differentials
            to have degree +1. For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V[n]
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            concentrated on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            in degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          #HirschExtension.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Hirsch extension of dg-modules)
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              be a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-module"} dg-module
              over
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              and let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}
              be a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hirsch+extension"} Hirsch extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphisms"} monomorphisms
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
              of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi N
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N \hookrightarrow (N \oplus (A \otimes V[n]), d_{\phi})
            %p given by a choice of
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi d
                          %mi V
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_V \;\colon\; V \to N_{n+1}
            %p
              where the differential
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_{\phi}
              is
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_N
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi N
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_A
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi
              followed by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/action"} action
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ρ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \rho
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              on
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi A
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi v
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi a
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi ρ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d_\phi (a \otimes v) = (d_A a) \otimes v + (-1)^{\vert a \vert}  \rho(a,\phi(v))
                    \\,.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Roig94"}> Roig 94, def. 1.8
            )
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              It follows that for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_1, N_2
              two
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
              then homomorphisms
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
              out of a Hirsch extension of the former (def.
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HirschExtension"}
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi ϕ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    f
                    \\;\colon\;
                    (N_1 \oplus (A \otimes V[n]), d_\phi)
                    \\longrightarrow
                    N_2
            %p is equivalently
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  a homomorphism of dg-modules
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi h
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mn 1
                          %mo →
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \colon N_1 \to N_2
              %li
                %p
                  a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi g
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                        %mi V
                        %mo →
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi N
                          %mn 2
                        %msub
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g \colon V \to (N_2)_{n}
            %p such that
            %ul
              %li
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi h
                      %mo ∘
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi ϕ
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi N
                            %mn 2
                      %mo ∘
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} h \circ d_{\phi} = d_{N_2} \circ g
                \.
          %p
            The following defines a kind of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+cofibrations"} minimal cofibrations
            of dg-modules.
          #KSFactorization.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (minimal KS-extension)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-module"} dg-module
              over
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+KS-extension"} minimal KS-extension
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              is a certain
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/transfinite+composition"} transfinite composition
              of Hirsch extensions, namely a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                    %mo ↪
                    %mover
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    N \hookrightarrow \hat N
            %p
              equipped with an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exhaustive+filtration"} exhaustive filtration
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mover
                      %mi N
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo ,
                    %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{\hat N(n,q)\}_{n,q \in \mathbb{N}}
              such that:
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ≃
                        %mi N
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat N(0,0) \simeq N
                  ;
              %li
                %p
                  the inclusions
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mover
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ↪
                        %mover
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hat N(n,q) \hookrightarrow \hat N(n,q+1)
                  are Hirsch extensions (def.
                  = succeed ")." do
                    %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#HirschExtension"}
              %li
                %p
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi N
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 0
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %msub
                          %munder
                            %mi lim
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mi q
                        %mover
                          %mi N
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ^
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi q
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N(n+1,0) = \underset{\longrightarrow}{\lim}_q \hat N(n,q)
                  (
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
                  over the sequence of Hirsch extensions in the previous degree).
            %p
              Accordingly, a
              %strong minimal KS-factorization
              of a morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 1
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N_1 \to N_2
              of
              = succeed "-dg-modules" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mn 1
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ⟶
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mn 2
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mrow
                              %mpadded{:lspace => "-100%width", :width => "0"}
                                %mfrac{:linethickness => "0"}
                                  %mrow
                                    %mtext minimal
                                  %mrow
                                    %mtext KS-extension
                            %mo ↘
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mo ↗
                              %mpadded{:width => "0"}
                                %mtext quasi-iso
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi N
                              %mn 1
                            %mo ⊕
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi V
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    N _1 &amp;&amp; \longrightarrow &amp;&amp; N_2
                    \\\
                    \&amp; {}_{\mathllap{\text{minimal} \atop \text{KS-extension}}}\searrow &amp;&amp; \nearrow_{\mathrlap{\text{quasi-iso}}}
                    \\\
                    \&amp;&amp; N_1 \oplus (A \otimes V)
                    }
                    \\,.
            %p
              Finally a
              %strong minimal KS-model
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-module"} dg-module
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \hookrightarrow N
              is a minimal KS-fibration.
          %p
            (
            %a{:href => "#Roig94"}> Roig 94, def. 1.9
            )
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              Let the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ground+field"} ground field
              be of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+zero"} characteristic zero
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f \colon N_1 \longrightarrow N_2
              be a morphism of
              = succeed "-" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-modules"} dg-modules
              such that it induces a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monomorphism"} monomorphism
              in degree-0
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %msup
                      %mi H
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi N
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H^0(f) \colon H^0(N_1) \hookrightarrow H^0(N_2)
              then it admits a minimal KS-factorization (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KSFactorization"}
            %p
              In particular, every
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-module"} dg-module
              has a minimal KS-model (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#KSFactorization"}
          %p
            %a{:href => "#RoigSaralegiAranguren00"} Roig &amp; Saralegi-Aranguren 00, theorem 1.3.1
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a{:href => "4-sphere#CircleAction"} 4-sphere – circle action
          %h2#related_entries Related entries
